objective:
Implement FOUNDATION ONLY for BB's standalone compact PWA navigation in the shared workspace. Read and obey AGENTS.md. Do not invoke Model Relay. Preserve .context/ and .impeccable.md. Use apply_patch for edits.

Scope:
1. Add one tested useStandaloneCompactPwa capability/helper using @bb/shared-ui compact viewport plus (display-mode: standalone), with safe iOS navigator.standalone fallback. No unsafe internal casts; parse at browser boundary.
2. Add a validated compact Command Center navigation state contract (return path/pane metadata as needed) and a pure policy deciding when new-thread/root route reconciliation must preserve the existing split layout.
3. Apply that policy in SplitThreadArea: only a validated standalone-compact Command Center commit to "/" skips reconcileLayoutForContent. Preview isn't part of this stage. Direct "/" and every non-standalone route keep current behavior. Add positive preservation and negative gate tests.
4. In sidebar.tsx, disable existing global right-swipe and wheel-to-open only when the capability is true. Button opening and Vaul swipe-to-close stay. Compact Safari-tab behavior remains. Add a test for PWA suppression and preserve existing browser swipe test.
5. Do not implement workspace swipe/transition UI yet. Do not change server/daemon contracts.
6. Run focused tests and pnpm exec turbo run typecheck --filter=@bb/app. Follow AGENTS Turbo rules. Report files, checks, exact limitations.

Acceptance:
- capability covers matchMedia standalone and iOS fallback;
- validated intent cannot be accidentally triggered by arbitrary location state;
- preserved layout keeps pane count/content/focus when Command Center route commits;
- non-standalone root reconcile still focuses/replaces exactly as today;
- PWA sidebar swipe and wheel cannot open, browser compact swipe still can;
- typecheck passes or evidence is reported.
